  "english": "May 9.\nThursday, Tone 8 [DK / Dg]. Ascension of Christ. [lc. 30].\nAnd everything else according to order.\nIn June\nSunday, Tone 2 [AK / Ab]. Coming of the Holy Spirit (Pentecost).\nEve of the Fast of Elijah.\nSunday, Tone 1 [AH / Aa]. First. Beginning of the Resurrection Sundays. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 1 [a3 / ad]: \"Who came for salvation.\"\n16.\nIn July\nSunday, Tone 4 [BK / Bb]. Sixth. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 4 [b3 / bd]: \"Who descended from heaven.\" Eve of the Fast of the Transfiguration [Vardavar]. 17. 21.\nSunday, Tone 3 [BZ / Bg]. Transfiguration [Vardavar]. The period of non-fasting is three weeks. See in the First Volume up to the Friday of the second week, and on Saturday come here. But see the daily readings here.\nIn August\nSunday, Tone 2 [AK / Ab]. Second. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 4 [bk / bc]: \"Who in the heavenly.\" 30.\nSaturday, Tone 8 [DK / Dg]. Holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\nSunday, Tone 1 [AZ / Ag]. Third. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 5 [g3 / gd]: \"We glorify.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 1 [ad / aa]: \"Glory to Thy Resurrection.\" Eve of the Fast of the Assumption of the Mother of God. 1.\nMonday, Tone 2 [AK / Ab]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 2 [ak / ab]: \"Ineffable essence.\" 2.\nSunday, Tone 8 [DK / Dg]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The period of non-fasting is three weeks. See in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\nSeptember\nSunday, Tone 5 [GZ / Gg]. Fourth. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 6 [gk / gc]: \"Ineffable.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 5 [g3 / gd]: \"Oil-bearing [women]\" and \"Today the Resurrection.\" Eve of the Fast of the Holy Cross. 14.\nMonday, Tone 6 [GK / Gc]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Virgin from Anna. 21.\nTuesday, Tone 7 [DZ / Da]. Fast. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 4 [bk / bc]: \"Who of our fathers.\"\nSunday, Tone 4 [BK / Bb]. Exaltation of the Cross [Khachverats]. See in the First Volume up to the tenth Sunday. But for the Father [Harts] hymns of the martyrs and of the fasts, and the Resurrection Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi] hymns and the daily tones, see the Year-book, keeping [the track of] this month.\nNovember\nSunday, Tone 3 [BZZ / Bg]. Tenth. Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 3 [b3 / bd]: \"The voice of good tidings\" to the end. Eve of the Fast of the Fifty Days [Yisnakats].\nMonday, Tone 4 [BK / Bb]. Fast of the Fifty Days. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 6 [gk / gc]: \"God most high.\"\nFriday, Tone 8 [DK / Dg]. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\nSunday, Tone 2 [AK / Ab]. First. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 1 [ad / aa]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 2 [ak / ab]: \"Risen\" and \"The wondrous angel.\"\nMonday, Tone 3 [BZ / Bg]. [Feast of] Julian and Vasiluhi. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 2 [ak / ab]: \"Holy God, creator.\"\nSunday, Tone 1 [AZ / Ag]. Second. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 2 [ak / ab]: \"Who for our salvation.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 1 [ay / aa]: \"Who by ineffable essence.\"\nDecember\nMonday, Tone 2 [AK / Ab]. [Feast of] Gennarius, and Mercurius, and Yakovkos [James], and Iragatar.\nTuesday, Tone 3 [BZ / Bg]. [Feast of] Cornelius the Centurion, and Shmavon [Simeon], etc.\nSunday, Tone 8 [DK / Dg]. Third. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 3 [bd / bg]: \"Incorruptible.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 8 [dk / dg]: \"Thy angel, Lord.\" Eve of the Fast of Holy James [St. James of Nisibis].\nTuesday, Tone 2 [AK / Ab]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\nWednesday, Tone 3 [BZ / Bg]. Fast. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 7 [dz / da]: \"Lord our God, who established.\"\nSunday, Tone 7 [DZ / Da]. Fourth. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 4 [bk / bc]: \"Unoriginate God.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn], Tone 5 [g3 / gd]: \"Who descended.\"\nSunday, Tone 6 [GK / Gc]. Fifth. Father [Harts hymn], Tone 5 [g3 / gd]: \"Glorified Son of God.\" Lord, I Have Cried [Hambartsi hymn]...",
